## Architecture and validator contract

Higher-level parameter handling already owns parameter-key resolution,
unknown-key handling, required/missing/default orchestration,
`parameterStructureKey` resolution and aggregation of validation results.

Preserve:

```js
{{ validate_function_name }}({
  value,
  parameter,
  context,
})
```

Valid:

```js
{ ok: true, value: normalizedValue }
```

Ordinary invalid user value:

```js
{
  ok: false,
  message: "Human-readable validation message",
  value,
}
```

Do NOT throw for ordinary invalid user values.

Only throw for genuine application/runtime invariant failures. For those use:

```text
Backend/utils/common/errors.js
```

```js
createInternalError(message, { field, details });
```

instead of plain Error/TypeError.

Reuse shared helpers when semantics match:

```text
Backend/utils/common/objects.js
  isPlainObject(value)
  hasOwnKey(object, key)

Backend/utils/common/strings.js
  normalizeNonEmptyString(value)
  isNonEmptyString(value)
```

Do not recreate equivalent generic helpers.

Backend context is:

```js
{
  modelName,
  leafCriteria,
  alternatives,
}
```

It intentionally differs from Frontend `parameterContext`.

## Expression Domains

